# Web styling: Tailwind + antdv colors

## Do

- Layout, spacing, typography, and one-off chrome: **Tailwind utility classes** on the template (`class` / `:class`)
- **Colors** from Ant Design — not ad-hoc hex/rgb in Vue:
  - Runtime tokens: `theme.useToken()` from `ant-design-vue/es` (`token.colorPrimary`, `colorText`, …)
  - Palettes: exports from `@ant-design/colors` (typed package exports only)
  - Wire shared brand colors into Tailwind via `@theme` in `apps/web/src/assets/main.css` using those same antd values when needed
- Prefer antdv components for forms, tables, modals, feedback; Tailwind for page/layout around them

## Do not

- `<style>`, `<style scoped>`, or extra `.vue` CSS modules for app UI
- Inline `style="..."` / `:style` object maps for colors/layout (exception: values that **must** come from `token` at runtime — prefer CSS variables / class bindings when possible)
- Hand-rolled custom CSS class names (`.my-card`, `.page-title`, …) in SFCs or side CSS files
- Random hex/palette outside antdv / `@ant-design/colors`

## Allowed CSS files

- `apps/web/src/assets/main.css` — Tailwind entry (`@import 'tailwindcss'`, optional `@theme` bridging antd colors)
- `ant-design-vue/dist/reset.css` (or ConfigProvider theme) — not a place for feature styles

## Example

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { blue } from '@ant-design/colors';
// Prefer token in app shell; palette import when mapping into @theme / constants
</script>

<template>
  <div class="flex min-h-screen flex-col gap-4 p-6">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--ant-color-text)]">Roles</h1>
  </div>
</template>
```

If a visual cannot be expressed with Tailwind + antd tokens, extend `@theme` / ConfigProvider — do not add a `<style>` block.
